---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import Link from "../components/Link.astro";
import { analyticsEvents, sessionContextProperties, vendorSections } from "../components/privacy/privacyPolicyModel";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, DOMAIN, ORGANISATION, POSTAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/privacy/organisation";
import { VENDORS } from "../lib/privacy/registry";

const vendors = vendorSections();
const hosting = VENDORS["github-pages"];
const analytics = VENDORS["google-analytics"];
const events = analyticsEvents();
const contextProperties = sessionContextProperties();
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${DOMAIN} handles personal data, who we share it with, and your rights.`}>
	<h2>Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		{ORGANISATION} ("we", "us") runs {DOMAIN}, a collection of free writing tools. To ask us anything about your data,
		email <Link href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</Link> or write to us at {POSTAL_ADDRESS}.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>
		This site is not directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If we
		learn that we have, we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>What we don't do</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>There are no accounts, and we don't ask for your name or email address.</li>
		<li>We don't show advertising or track you across other websites.</li>
		<li>We don't sell your data.</li>
		<li>We don't use personal data to train AI models.</li>
		<li>
			We don't receive what you write. It stays on your device, and when a tool makes a share link, the link carries
			your text after the <code>#</code> in the address, which browsers never send to a server.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Hosting</h2>
	<p>
		{hosting.name} serves this site. When you visit, {hosting.name} logs your IP address for security and to keep the
		service running, as described in <Link href={hosting.privacyUrl}>its privacy statement</Link>. Our legal basis is
		legitimate interest: a website can't be delivered or protected without this. GitHub keeps these logs; we don't receive them.
	</p>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>
	<p>
		If you accept, we use {analytics.name} to understand which tools and settings people use, so we know what to improve.
		Our legal basis is your consent. Nothing is loaded until you accept, and you can withdraw consent at any time.
	</p>
	<p>
		In plain terms, we record which tool settings you use, roughly how long your text is (in ranges of word counts),
		how you reach the site, how long you use a tool, and your device type. We never record what you write.
		Google also receives what it collects automatically, such as your IP address and browser details. For the cookies
		involved and how long they last, see the <Link href="/cookie-policy">cookie policy</Link>.
	</p>
	<details>
		<summary>The exact events we send</summary>
		<ul class="events">
			{
				events.map((event) => (
					<li>
						<code>{event.name}</code>
						{event.properties.length > 0 && <span>: {event.properties.join(", ")}</span>}
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
		<p>
			Every event also includes: {contextProperties.join(", ")}.
		</p>
	</details>
	<p><Button variant="secondary" data-open-cookie-settings>Change your cookie settings</Button></p>

	<h2>Who we share data with</h2>
	<ul class="vendors">
		{
			vendors.map((vendor) => (
				<li>
					<strong>{vendor.name}</strong> ({vendor.category}). {vendor.roleDescription}{" "}
					<Link href={vendor.privacyUrl}>Privacy policy</Link>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<p>We may also disclose personal data:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>To comply with the law, a court order or a government or regulatory request.</li>
		<li>To protect the rights, property or safety of us, our users or others.</li>
		<li>To a successor, if we are part of a merger, acquisition or sale of assets.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>International transfers</h2>
	<p>These companies may process data outside your country. We rely on the following safeguards:</p>
	<ul>
		{
			vendors.map((vendor) => (
				<li>
					{vendor.name}: {vendor.transfer}
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		Depending on where you live, you may be able to ask us for access to the personal data we hold about you, to correct
		or delete it, to restrict or object to how we use it, to receive a portable copy, and to withdraw your consent. If
		you are in the EU or UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority. We don't sell personal data
		or use it for targeted advertising, so there is nothing to opt out of.
	</p>
	<p>
		To exercise a right, email <Link href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</Link>. Analytics data is linked
		only to a random ID stored in your browser, not to your name, so we usually can't find one person's data. If you want us to
		try, tell us the value of the <code>_ga</code> cookie from your browser. Turning analytics off in the cookie settings
		stops any further collection.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you are in the EU or UK, our legal bases are your consent for analytics, and our legitimate interest in running
		and securing the site for hosting. If a browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a refusal of
		analytics. We don't respond to Do Not Track, as there is no common standard for it.
	</p>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>
		We use reasonable measures to protect personal data from loss and unauthorised access. No system is completely secure, so we can't guarantee the security of
		anything sent over the internet.
	</p>

	<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
	<p>
		We keep personal data only as long as we need it for the purposes above. The cookies we set last as long as the{" "}
		<Link href="/cookie-policy">cookie policy</Link> says, and you can delete them at any time in your browser.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>We update this page when what we collect or who we share it with changes. The date at the top shows the latest change.</p>
</LegalPage>

<style>
	ul {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
		padding-inline-start: var(--space-6);
	}
	li {
		margin-block-end: var(--space-2);
	}
	details {
		margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
	}
	summary {
		cursor: pointer;
		margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
	}
	.events {
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}
</style>
